# 25. Final Takeaways

Before moving forward, I should be able to recognize these patterns quickly:

```text
One loop
→ O(n)

Nested n loops
→ O(n²)

Separate loops
→ O(n)

Repeated doubling / halving
→ O(log n)

n combined with log n
→ O(n log n)

Linear recursion
→ O(n) time, O(n) space

Naive recursive Fibonacci
→ O(2^n) time, O(n) space

Binary Search
→ O(log n) time, O(1) space
```

The goal is not to memorize hundreds of formulas.

The goal is to **look at code and understand how the amount of work and memory changes when `n` becomes larger**.

